# Loaded BEFORE .env for `pnpm --filter @spine/api test:integration` only
# (see apps/api/package.json's own script — dotenv-cli's -e flag is
# first-file-wins for a given key, not last, so this file's DATABASE_URL
# must be passed before .env's to actually take effect) — overrides
# DATABASE_URL to a separate, dedicated database on the same local
# Postgres server.
#
# Why this file exists: apps/api/src/db/ledger-integrity.integration.test.ts
# (and any future integration test) TRUNCATEs real tables — including
# `organization ... CASCADE`, which deletes every org/membership in
# whatever database it's pointed at — as part of its own cleanup. Before
# this file existed, integration tests ran against the SAME database as
# local dev (both just read `.env`), so running the test suite silently
# wiped every real dev org/user, including active sessions, as a side
# effect of test cleanup. This was diagnosed live after a real account got
# wiped repeatedly during a debugging session investigating exactly this
# symptom, before the actual cause (this file's absence) was found.
#
# `spine_test` must exist on the same Postgres server `DATABASE_URL` in
# `.env` points at, and have the same schema applied
# (`pnpm --filter @spine/api db:migrate` against this URL, or create it
# via `createdb spine_test` and re-run migrations). CI is unaffected — it
# spins up its own single-use Postgres container per run regardless (see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml), so this override is a no-op there in
# practice, but harmless either way since CI's ephemeral DB has nothing
# real to lose.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://spine:spine@localhost:5432/spine_test
